{
  "dom_id": "step-q51569",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14230523/assets/be6a289223fdd6c6896278b5e179bf9f4a98d7f9e5988d1b5ae98a1217dd48b0.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Given that $y=f(x)$ is periodic with period $3,$ what is the value of $f(30)?$",
  "worked_solution": "Since the period is $3,$ if we add (or subtract) any multiple of $3$ from the input, the output stays the same.\n\nSo, we can keep subtracting $3$ from the input until we get to an input that we see in the graph:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(30) & =f(30-3) \\\\  & =f(30-2\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =⋯ \\\\  & =f(30-10\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =f(0) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
